# core/dependents-direct - Transitive dependents, via the direct predicate form.
#
# Answers: everything that reaches the focus element at any depth by following the
# predicates you named.
#
# Does NOT prove: impact, criticality or failure propagation - and not
# completeness either, because it follows only the predicates given. A dependency
# expressed through a relationship type you left out is silently absent.
#
# REQUIRES capabilities.direct_rel_triples. Current converters emit these triples
# wherever the notation publishes a predicate. Older output, or conversion with
# --no-emit-direct-rel-triples, requires the qualified reading instead.
# Unlike core/dependents (two hops over all declared relationship predicates),
# this follows only PREDICATE_PATH at any depth. Potential derivations assert no
# triple and are not traversed.
#
# Never union these rows with core/neighbours-qualified. When direct triples are
# emitted, every relationship exists in both forms, so a union double-counts and
# nothing raises an error.
#
# PREDICATE_PATH is an alternation, capped, and required. Get the predicates from
# core/reified-predicates rather than assuming which ones this dataset uses; the
# notation ontologies are versioned in the namespace, so am: and am4: spell the same
# concept differently.
#
# NOT from core/discover-relationship-types, which this used to recommend. That
# template reports the qualified relationship CLASSES a dataset uses - am:Serving,
# bpmn:SequenceFlow - and this parameter needs the unqualified PREDICATES those
# classes stand for - am:serves. Following a class as if it were a predicate matches
# nothing, and returns it as an empty answer rather than an error. core/reified-
# predicates reads the rdf:reifies bridge, whose triple term names exactly the
# predicate each relationship stands for, which is the same bridge whose presence
# gates this template.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, PREDICATE_PATH, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT DISTINCT ?dependent ?dependentLabel
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
    ?dependent ({{PREDICATE_PATH}})+ ?focus .
    FILTER(?dependent != ?focus)
    OPTIONAL { ?dependent {{PATH:label}} ?dependentLabel }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?dependentLabel ?dependent
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
